Kind: ablation
Issue: #951
Takes out: the boot run by run-x86_64.sh as a job waited for -- it runs in the foreground again, as before #951, and a shell runs a trap only once the command it waits for in the foreground has ended: ablate.sh sent SIGTERM during a paused boot goes on until that boot's 120 s of silence are out.  harness-lifecycle-check.sh's abstop finds ablate.sh still running 30 s after SIGTERM.
Script: scripts/harness-lifecycle-check.sh
Script: --only
Script: abstop
Expect: lifecycle: abstop: .* -- WRONG
Note: run under each accelerator ablate.sh is given, which passes --kvm to harness-lifecycle-check.sh under KVM; abstop's probe is booted by run-x86_64.sh, the third of the three ways a boot is made, and only that way is taken back to the foreground, its status handed to the wait by a job already over

